      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iron_City%2C_Tennessee"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "When it first grew, Iron City sat on the edge of Lawrence and Wayne counties, spilling into both.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iron_City%2C_Tennessee"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Iron ore mining really took off in 1886 when a railroad line reached the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iron_City%2C_Tennessee"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A 1877 state act shifted the county line so that Iron City became entirely part of Lawrence County before it officially incorporated.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
